WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.603
- Why is your red meat video offline?

00:00:04.116 --> 00:00:06.783
(upbeat music)

00:00:08.470 --> 00:00:09.770
Victoria, thanks for asking.

00:00:09.770 --> 00:00:12.340
A lot of people have been
speculating about this actually.

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:13.840
The reason I had to take the video down is

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:15.210
because there was some confusion

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:16.930
between the sponsor and myself

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:19.490
about what they were
comfortable with having

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:21.570
within the video as far as content goes.

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:23.420
And they wanted me to change something

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:24.690
once I posted the video.

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:28.090
Me being a person who stands
behind my medical ethics

00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:30.670
and didn't want to change
my medical opinion,

00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:32.760
we came to a mutual agreement

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:34.350
that we just take the video down.

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:36.620
What I want to say
about the red meat video

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:40.310
is that I still very much
stand behind everything I said.

00:00:40.310 --> 00:00:41.920
You should dramatically reduce,

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:44.180
if not remove entirely processed meats,

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:46.180
and if you have them once in a while,

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:47.640
that's not a major risk

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:49.240
that you should be really worrying about.

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:52.280
Yes, overeating red meats
is not probably not ideal,

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:55.260
but eating them in moderation
alongside vegetables,

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:57.070
and especially preparing
them in the right way

00:00:57.070 --> 00:00:59.770
like I said, marinating
them, not overcooking them

00:00:59.770 --> 00:01:02.780
probably reduces a lot of these
negative effects we've seen

00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:03.840
in some of the research.

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:05.570
And if you choose not to eat meat

00:01:05.570 --> 00:01:07.390
because of ethical reasons,

00:01:07.390 --> 00:01:09.460
more power to you, that's your decision.

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:11.950
But it doesn't mean
that you have to come at

00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:13.230
and yell at other people

00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:15.470
who don't necessarily
see eye to eye with you.

00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:17.880
Whenever I make a video, sponsored or not,

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:20.550
I wanna give you my true, honest opinion.

00:01:20.550 --> 00:01:23.570
I take that trust you
give me very seriously.

00:01:23.570 --> 00:01:26.110
I will never tell you
what someone else wants me

00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:27.880
to tell you, unless I stand behind it.

00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:31.420
Now that being said, I will
work with all sorts of sponsors

00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:34.180
as long as they are
letting me say my message

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:36.370
that I would say if the
video wasn't sponsored.

00:01:36.370 --> 00:01:40.050
Stop just doing dumbbell curls.

00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:42.370
You need to work out
the rest of your body.

00:01:42.370 --> 00:01:43.203
Thanks.

00:01:43.203 --> 00:01:45.980
Johnathon, I actually don't
do dumbbell curls at all.

00:01:45.980 --> 00:01:48.410
I'm a firm believer in
doing compound lifts.

00:01:48.410 --> 00:01:50.800
In reality, the way that
these guns come about.

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:51.633
I'm just kidding.

00:01:51.633 --> 00:01:53.970
Pull-ups, weighted pull-ups, I do rows.

00:01:53.970 --> 00:01:56.330
Those are the ways I
get my bicep workout in.

00:01:56.330 --> 00:01:58.200
I don't think you necessarily need to do

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:00.670
nor is it tremendously
effective to isolate the bicep

00:02:00.670 --> 00:02:01.540
and just do curls.

00:02:01.540 --> 00:02:04.110
Krissy Pooh: I wanna know
if this is normal or not.

00:02:04.110 --> 00:02:07.020
When I get sick my skin
gets painful to the touch.

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:08.530
Normal, the reason it's happening

00:02:08.530 --> 00:02:10.200
is probably because you have a fever.

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:13.560
And when you have a fever, your
skin becomes hypersensitive,

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:15.220
so anything touching it

00:02:15.220 --> 00:02:18.160
will feel like a weird, gross feeling.

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:19.750
And this probably evolved

00:02:19.750 --> 00:02:21.410
as some sort of survival mechanism.

00:02:21.410 --> 00:02:23.300
Totally normal, nothing to worry about,

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:25.470
as long as it's only
present while you're sick.

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:28.631
Lea Fa: What's your thought
on breast reduction?

00:02:28.631 --> 00:02:31.500
I mean, it depends why you're
getting breast reduction.

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:35.370
I have a lot of patients
who have very large breasts,

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:38.050
and because of that they
develop serious back problems

00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:39.510
'cause they're carrying so much weight.

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:41.740
Also, it can affect the
way that you see yourself

00:02:41.740 --> 00:02:43.770
as a person, so it can hurt you mentally.

00:02:43.770 --> 00:02:46.290
I agree that everyone is beautiful,

00:02:46.290 --> 00:02:48.257
but I also think it's unfair to say

00:02:48.257 --> 00:02:51.010
"Everyone should just be
totally happy with their bodies,

00:02:51.010 --> 00:02:51.843
as is."

00:02:51.843 --> 00:02:53.400
If someone has a bad scar

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:55.100
and they're feeling
self-conscious about it,

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:57.450
lying about it and just
saying that it's beautiful,

00:02:57.450 --> 00:02:59.100
trying to convince them otherwise,

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:00.110
a little bit unfair

00:03:00.110 --> 00:03:02.270
Some things make people
feel self conscious.

00:03:02.270 --> 00:03:05.380
So it's about getting an honest
history, a true physical,

00:03:05.380 --> 00:03:07.500
figuring out what the
risks and benefits are

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:08.600
of each procedure,

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:10.777
and making an individual
decision for yourself

00:03:10.777 --> 00:03:12.460
with your doctor.

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:15.340
Rashiekah Love Toshinori Yagi:

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:17.800
Is it normal for your lower rib to pop?

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:21.460
No, I'm not even really sure
how your lower rib would pop.

00:03:21.460 --> 00:03:23.350
The lower ribs are called false ribs

00:03:23.350 --> 00:03:25.830
'cause they're actually not
attached to your sternum,

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:29.270
they're just sort of
floating in your backside.

00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:30.810
Maybe they're rubbing against each other.

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:32.340
Maybe there is a tendon or ligament

00:03:32.340 --> 00:03:33.380
that's getting caught there.

00:03:33.380 --> 00:03:35.130
But if it's causing you discomfort,

00:03:35.130 --> 00:03:36.430
please go see your doctor

00:03:36.430 --> 00:03:38.710
because you really should
find out what that is.

00:03:38.710 --> 00:03:40.180
I've noticed when I get extra tired,

00:03:40.180 --> 00:03:43.270
I snore a lot and then I
wake up with a sore throat.

00:03:43.270 --> 00:03:45.610
Should I see a doctor about sleep apnea?

00:03:45.610 --> 00:03:48.180
Lindsay, you should
absolutely see your doctor

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:49.200
about sleep apnea,

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:52.410
because while sleep apnea
isn't an immediate threat,

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:54.070
it's one of these conditions

00:03:54.070 --> 00:03:56.700
that causes chronic hazard to your health.

00:03:56.700 --> 00:03:58.410
So you develop other medical problems

00:03:58.410 --> 00:04:01.000
like high blood pressure,
chronic heart disease.

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:03.660
If you can control your
sleep apnea early on,

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:06.360
the less of these other
diseases and complications

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:07.360
you're gonna develop later.

00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:08.600
My thing as a family doctor

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:11.300
is about preventing problems
before they become one.

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:12.860
And that's something you can totally do

00:04:12.860 --> 00:04:14.530
if you truly have sleep apnea.

00:04:14.530 --> 00:04:16.500
It sounds like you have sleep apnea,

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:17.820
especially if you're snoring to the point

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:18.770
of getting a sore throat.

00:04:18.770 --> 00:04:20.100
Dana Habib: Hey Doc.

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:21.800
So I'm about to graduate from high school

00:04:21.800 --> 00:04:22.970
and my dream is to work at

00:04:22.970 --> 00:04:25.050
either the ED or be a paramedic,

00:04:25.050 --> 00:04:27.810
but everyone is saying
that it's too traumatizing.

00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:28.780
Is that true?

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:32.000
Ah, Dana, I don't want
anyone to dissuade you

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:34.810
from entering a particular
field you're passionate about

00:04:34.810 --> 00:04:35.930
because in this life

00:04:35.930 --> 00:04:38.640
passion is hard to find at times,

00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:42.120
and especially in a field
that is incredibly rewarding

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:45.870
and a field that's incredibly
needed in our society,

00:04:45.870 --> 00:04:47.940
I don't think you should
let anyone dissuade you.

00:04:47.940 --> 00:04:50.920
What I think you should do
is you should go volunteer,

00:04:50.920 --> 00:04:53.590
you should go on a ride-along if you can,

00:04:53.590 --> 00:04:56.300
you should talk to folks who
actually work those jobs.

00:04:56.300 --> 00:04:58.050
Once you expose yourself to the field,

00:04:58.050 --> 00:05:00.420
you can have a better idea
if you truly love it or not.

00:05:00.420 --> 00:05:03.820
It's very easy to fall in love
with the idea of something,

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:05.420
but once you actually start doing it,

00:05:05.420 --> 00:05:06.870
you may not feel the same way.

00:05:06.870 --> 00:05:09.190
So I always say, "Firsthand experience

00:05:09.190 --> 00:05:11.400
trumps what anyone else is telling you."

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:14.280
So if you're passionate,
you wanna try it, go try it,

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:15.340
and then make your decision.

00:05:15.340 --> 00:05:16.910
Hey Mike, can you get stretch marks

00:05:16.910 --> 00:05:18.852
from losing weight too
fast? Love your channel.

00:05:18.852 --> 00:05:21.190
Yeah, actually what can happen is

00:05:21.190 --> 00:05:25.020
anytime you have a rapid change in weight,

00:05:25.020 --> 00:05:27.610
you can get unusual marks on your skin.

00:05:27.610 --> 00:05:29.910
I've had patients that
have had bariatric surgery,

00:05:29.910 --> 00:05:31.110
lost a lot of weight,

00:05:31.110 --> 00:05:33.520
not only do they get
stretch marks on their skin,

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:35.160
but they just have a lot of loose skin

00:05:35.160 --> 00:05:37.590
and end up needing
plastic surgery afterwards

00:05:37.590 --> 00:05:38.720
to get rid of that skin.

00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:39.553
Now that being said,

00:05:39.553 --> 00:05:42.450
you should still moisturize
your skin, that does help,

00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:45.780
don't splurge on the
100, 200 dollar creams

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:48.290
that promise you removal of stretch marks.

00:05:48.290 --> 00:05:51.720
Stretch marks, when you
grow rapidly in size

00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:52.760
and then shrink,

00:05:52.760 --> 00:05:55.740
actually come from a tearing
or scarring of the skin.

00:05:55.740 --> 00:05:57.670
No cream is really gonna fix that.

00:05:57.670 --> 00:05:59.360
Hurricane Devan: Hey Doctor Mike.

00:05:59.360 --> 00:06:01.320
So I recently got braces on my teeth

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:03.010
and my mouth is really sore and tender.

00:06:03.010 --> 00:06:05.290
Is there a way to help
me lower the pain quickly

00:06:05.290 --> 00:06:07.230
so I can chew harder foods again?

00:06:07.230 --> 00:06:08.440
I feel you.

00:06:08.440 --> 00:06:10.740
You know why? Because
I've had braces twice.

00:06:10.740 --> 00:06:13.560
First, when I was in high
school. I got a Invisalign.

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:16.420
And every two weeks, you had
to get a new plate put in

00:06:16.420 --> 00:06:17.720
and it would shift your teeth

00:06:17.720 --> 00:06:19.960
and it would be the most
painful, excruciating...

00:06:19.960 --> 00:06:22.530
Once I got older, my teeth
shifted a little bit,

00:06:22.530 --> 00:06:24.180
I had to get braces a second time,

00:06:24.180 --> 00:06:26.250
and I had to get real braces,

00:06:26.250 --> 00:06:28.740
like I had a metal mouth
while in medical school.

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:29.850
And it was a difficult moment

00:06:29.850 --> 00:06:31.360
because I wanted to look my best,

00:06:31.360 --> 00:06:33.860
but I also knew I was
investing in my future.

00:06:33.860 --> 00:06:37.030
A simple trick that I used
that worked well for me is

00:06:37.030 --> 00:06:40.430
there's some numbing agents
that work if you have like a

00:06:40.430 --> 00:06:43.260
sore in your mouth. Those
can work well sometimes,

00:06:43.260 --> 00:06:46.750
but in reality, the only solution is time.

00:06:46.750 --> 00:06:47.830
And I know it's horrible

00:06:47.830 --> 00:06:49.750
every time getting your braces tightened,

00:06:49.750 --> 00:06:51.750
and it comes with a huge amount of pain.

00:06:51.750 --> 00:06:54.260
So, first step, understand that this pain

00:06:54.260 --> 00:06:55.400
is not a threat to you.

00:06:55.400 --> 00:06:57.930
That alone can lower the
level of some of the pain.

00:06:57.930 --> 00:06:59.370
But there are some numbing agents

00:06:59.370 --> 00:07:01.890
that you can go and buy over
the counter in the pharmacy.

00:07:01.890 --> 00:07:03.560
Obviously, talk to your dentist first,

00:07:03.560 --> 00:07:05.320
but that could be a great way of treating

00:07:05.320 --> 00:07:07.030
the first day of pain that you get

00:07:07.030 --> 00:07:08.240
when you get your braces tightened.

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:10.383
Question: Tips for
someone with bad posture?

00:07:10.383 --> 00:07:13.060
Tat, this is actually pretty
funny cause a lot of people

00:07:13.060 --> 00:07:15.380
in my Curbside Consult video

00:07:15.380 --> 00:07:18.270
and in my Resident Reaction
video, where I toured the set

00:07:18.270 --> 00:07:20.900
with Manish Dayal, people
told me I had poor posture.

00:07:20.900 --> 00:07:24.080
I sometimes have poor posture
when I'm interviewing people,

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:27.440
mostly because I'm 6'3" and
most people are not 6'3".

00:07:27.440 --> 00:07:28.990
So I try to get on people's level

00:07:28.990 --> 00:07:30.760
and that does hurt my posture somewhat.

00:07:30.760 --> 00:07:32.530
But if you work with a physical therapist

00:07:32.530 --> 00:07:33.970
and retrain your muscles,

00:07:33.970 --> 00:07:35.860
you can actually improve your posture.

00:07:35.860 --> 00:07:38.240
Is there any way to induce your period?

00:07:38.240 --> 00:07:40.100
This is an interesting question, Jasmine.

00:07:40.100 --> 00:07:41.540
I don't know how old you are

00:07:41.540 --> 00:07:44.170
and I don't know if you've
ever had your period before.

00:07:44.170 --> 00:07:46.180
I'll give you sort of the
medical background on this.

00:07:46.180 --> 00:07:49.400
Primary Amenorrhea is someone, a girl,

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:51.040
who has never had her period.

00:07:51.040 --> 00:07:54.610
Secondary Amenorrhea is a secondary cause,

00:07:54.610 --> 00:07:56.380
meaning that you've
had your period before,

00:07:56.380 --> 00:07:58.330
but now something is influencing your body

00:07:58.330 --> 00:07:59.610
to not have a period.

00:07:59.610 --> 00:08:00.770
So I'm not sure

00:08:00.770 --> 00:08:03.420
what's causing you to
want to have your period.

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:05.250
Is it because you missed
it and you want it?

00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:07.100
It's irregular and you
want to make it regular?

00:08:07.100 --> 00:08:08.600
But this is a really good time for you

00:08:08.600 --> 00:08:09.750
to go see your doctor,

00:08:09.750 --> 00:08:12.810
have a conversation about
what it is you really want.

00:08:12.810 --> 00:08:15.090
Because its really hard to
give you a simple answer,

00:08:15.090 --> 00:08:17.150
when there's so many things
that could be going on.

00:08:17.150 --> 00:08:20.050
Both from a health perspective,
but also in your mind,

00:08:20.050 --> 00:08:21.720
why you wanna induce your period.

00:08:21.720 --> 00:08:24.270
So to answer your question,
can you induce a period?

00:08:24.270 --> 00:08:25.270
Technically, yes.

00:08:25.270 --> 00:08:26.700
It depends for what purposes,

00:08:26.700 --> 00:08:28.360
it depends on what stage of your life.

00:08:28.360 --> 00:08:30.560
Go see your doctor, have a conversation,

00:08:30.560 --> 00:08:32.390
and figure out what works best for you.

00:08:32.390 --> 00:08:33.970
What do the other doctors at your work

00:08:33.970 --> 00:08:34.845
think of your YouTube?

00:08:34.845 --> 00:08:37.840
Christopher, we don't talk about it much.

00:08:37.840 --> 00:08:39.640
The senior doctors that I've worked with

00:08:39.640 --> 00:08:42.990
in the last five years, they
always ask what I'm up to.

00:08:42.990 --> 00:08:46.260
They love hearing the
successes that I'm having

00:08:46.260 --> 00:08:48.070
because they know how passionate I am

00:08:48.070 --> 00:08:49.230
and how hard I work,

00:08:49.230 --> 00:08:51.550
because I know you only
see what's happening

00:08:51.550 --> 00:08:53.360
on YouTube or on social media,

00:08:53.360 --> 00:08:54.438
but behind the scenes

00:08:54.438 --> 00:08:57.220
it takes a lot of work
to make this happen.

00:08:57.220 --> 00:08:59.132
Not only does it take a lot
of work to make this happen,

00:08:59.132 --> 00:09:02.160
I never let my work in the hospital

00:09:02.160 --> 00:09:04.320
or my patients suffer
because I'm busy here.

00:09:04.320 --> 00:09:07.210
They're a priority, I love being a doctor,

00:09:07.210 --> 00:09:09.160
and being one-on-one in
a room with a patient.

00:09:09.160 --> 00:09:11.490
So I make sure all my work is done there,

00:09:11.490 --> 00:09:13.760
prior to doing anything with social media.

00:09:13.760 --> 00:09:16.640
So they respect me, they appreciate it,

00:09:16.640 --> 00:09:18.640
they love that I'm
battling misinformation.

00:09:18.640 --> 00:09:21.400
And hopefully, if this podcast
that we've talked about

00:09:21.400 --> 00:09:23.310
in the past ever comes to fruition,

00:09:23.310 --> 00:09:25.010
maybe I can get them to guest on the show.

00:09:25.010 --> 00:09:27.480
Drop your questions and
comments down below.

00:09:27.480 --> 00:09:29.398
As always, stay happy and healthy.

00:09:29.398 --> 00:09:31.981
(upbeat music)

